    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2LMHWajjsQhzXYP7865LdcB)_\n\n## What\n- `sp-litnotes-meta-add-all-tables` now puts a `* Sections` heading above the table block, with a blank line before and after the heading.\n- The command can be re-run to complete notes: it adds only what is missing.\n  - No heading and no block: both go above the first heading.\n  - A block above the first heading, no heading: the heading is added above the block.\n  - The heading without a block: the block goes under it.\n  - A block under another heading: left alone.\n- `refresh-all-tables` and `backfill-children` share the same insert function, so they behave the same.\n- `C-u` dry run still previews; notes that would only get the heading are listed separately.\n\n## Testing\n- Emacs 29.3 batch: all 63 ERT tests in `sp-litnotes-meta-test.el` pass, including a new test for each state and for a second run changing nothing.\n- Tangle of the literate doc matches the committed `.el`.\n- Not run on the real vault.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDRDUFkqHUuvoUQ5Zc)_",
